{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Poverty and shame</b> — that others will shame him. <b>Both shall come to a man</b> — he shall exact retribution. מוסר is in the sense of מפרע (payment on credit)." "<b>But he who keeps reproof</b> — that they will reprove him." "<b>Shall be honored</b> — that HaShem will honor him, as in the verse: 'those who honor Me I will honor.'"], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "The comment on 'both shall come' is compressed; the hyper-literal rendering preserves the abruptness. The second sentence on מוסר/מפרע juxtaposes the terms without connective tissue, as in the original."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:36.240695599Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}